notes/suffmap_results.md-227-**Status.**
notes/suffmap_results.md-228-- (a) is KNOWN (Pomerance's L(X)^{√2}). The size principle itself, and hence σ = 2α in L-units, is stated explicitly in
notes/suffmap_results.md-229-  Pomerance 2008 (MSRI 44, eq. (8) and §"A general principle, a moral, and three bullets", p. 78): the analysis
notes/suffmap_results.md-230-  "can serve, in an almost intact manner, for many factoring algorithms. What may change is the number X."
notes/suffmap_results.md:231:- The matching exponent-level lower bound for random squares is Pomerance, ICM 1994 (Birkhäuser 1995, pp. 411–422),
notes/suffmap_results.md-232-  sharpened to constants by CGPT 2012. The lemma number in the ICM paper is not checked.
notes/suffmap_results.md-233-- The exponent bookkeeping α = (1+α)/2-type is heurnfs B5.
notes/suffmap_results.md-234-- The fixed-point form c^{2−b} = 4αA, the ω-independence for single families, and (e) are our packaging. No prior
notes/suffmap_results.md-235-  statement was found by us. They are routine.
