notes/suffmap_results.md-410-
notes/suffmap_results.md-411-**E1. A sampling family whose law gives C* = O(F_α), α < 1/3.**
notes/suffmap_results.md-412-- *Statement.* An L^{o(1)}-enumerable family whose law has C* ≤ cF_α, α < 1/3, with O(1) smoothness integers per
notes/suffmap_results.md-413-  candidate and a ring-map or congruence link.
notes/suffmap_results.md-414-- *Gives* L[α, c]. *Extra:* H_S, R.
notes/suffmap_results.md-415-- *Relation.*
notes/suffmap_results.md-416-  - ⇔ (within model S) any sub-1/3 sampling method (Theorem SS).
notes/suffmap_results.md-417-  - Instances:
notes/suffmap_results.md:418:    - E1a, the rank-r aggregate linked module: two degree-d ≍ √x fields, r ≍ x^{1/4} linked elements, family height
notes/suffmap_results.md:419:      N^{1/d}; formally 1/4 (resbarrier §4.2);
notes/suffmap_results.md-420-    - E1b, toric / entropy–height separation (heurnfs §5(i)).
notes/suffmap_results.md-421-  - Recognised neighbours: Schmidt's counts of algebraic points of bounded height, used as the heuristic G_r.
notes/suffmap_results.md-422-- *Believed* false for typical N. G_r predicts N^{e} families with e ≤ 1 − (r−1)(1 − 1/d) < 0, and none is
notes/suffmap_results.md-423-  constructed.
notes/suffmap_results.md-424-- *Implication:* model-PROVED.
