notes/suffmap_results.md-657-## 3. High-profile candidates: sufficient, necessary, or unrelated
notes/suffmap_results.md-658-
notes/suffmap_results.md-659-| # | candidate | verdict | precise reason |
notes/suffmap_results.md-660-|---|---|---|---|
notes/suffmap_results.md-661-| H1 | Matomäki–Radziwiłł 2016 (Cor. 1: X^ε-smooth in [X, X + C√X]; Cor. 6: almost all intervals); Hildebrand, Friedlander–Granville, Croot, Matomäki, Jain 2025 (small y). Harper's papers are on APs and minor arcs, not short intervals | **irrelevant to speed**: yields no algorithm and is used by none; relevant to *rigour* | Existence theorems at y = X^ε carry no algorithm. Factoring needs y = X^{o(1)}. Their L-scale analogues are the *existence half* of C1/C2's promise routes (Prop PC) and inputs to rigorous relation supply (the project's Theorem U uses Drappeau/Harper for smooth numbers in APs; Lee–Venkatesan 2018 for rigorous NFS) |
notes/suffmap_results.md-662-| H2 | "every [x, x + x^ε] contains an x^ε-smooth number" | **unrelated** (stated in Granville 2008 §1.2/§4.4, who shows it implies Vinogradov's least-nonresidue conjecture for p ≡ 3 mod 4) | wrong scale: positive density ρ(1/ε), y = x^ε; no construction |
notes/suffmap_results.md:663:| H3 | deterministic construction of a y-smooth integer in a given interval | **sufficient**: 1.2114 at (X ≈ kN, h = L_X[2/3, ν], y = L_X[1/3, κ], ν > 2/(3κ)) (Prop SI); 1.6386 at NFS rational rows if complete or with h₀ ≈ gap (Lemma SL, Prop PC); **heuristic poly time** in the Bohr-set form. **Insufficient** for exponent < 1/3 in single-interval form | §1.3–1.4 |
notes/suffmap_results.md-664-| H4 | Polymath4 (deterministic primes in [x, 2x]; Tao–Croot–Helfgott 2012) | **unrelated** in the sufficient direction | primes are dense (1/log x) and need no smoothness; the smooth analogue is H3 |
notes/suffmap_results.md-665-| H5 | sum-product (Erdős–Szemerédi; Bourgain–Katz–Tao; Chang) | **unrelated** | These are *upper* bounds on additive structure of multiplicative sets. They are consistent with H and too weak to bound box counts below H's prediction. Inverse theorems (PFR) concern small doubling, which box values lack |
notes/suffmap_results.md-666-| H6 | expansion of Cay((Z/N)^*, small primes) (GRH) | existence of short paths, diameter and mixing **unrelated**, since they yield no algorithm. (Abundance of collisions, nonexact Prop AB, is a different statement: collisions can lie in a proper subgroup.) **Constructive navigation sufficient**. It is DL mod N relative to a factor base, so it is KNOWN in substance (Bach 1984: DL mod N ⇒ factoring); GRH expansion is Jao–Miller–Venkatesan 2009: randomized polynomial time, PROVED with no heuristic (E3(iii), codex) | generic-group bounds make navigation without integer structure exponential |
notes/suffmap_results.md:667:| H7 | number fields of small discriminant with a prescribed root mod N (Kirchner; resbarrier) | **sufficient for constants only** (≤ 1.5263 two-map, 1.2114 ramified); never an exponent (C2/RB2) | heights refuted for almost all N (GAE, GAE-ram); discriminant version open |
notes/suffmap_results.md-668-| H8 | abc; S-unit counts (Evertse 1984; Erdős–Stewart–Tijdeman 1988; Lagarias–Soundararajan's xyz conjecture) | **unrelated** | With S = primes ≤ B, rad(uv) ≤ e^{B(1+o(1))}, so abc is vacuous for u − v = kN. Evertse's 3·7^{3+2s} (s finite primes; his count includes the infinite place) is exp(O(B)). Existence is not the bottleneck (S²/N − S pairs, nonexact Prop AB). *Algorithmic* S-unit solving is **sufficient** (E3). abcsunit Props ABCV/EV agree: abc is automatically satisfied unless the relation is unusually powerful, and Evertse counts only the triply-smooth subfamily |
notes/suffmap_results.md-669-| H9 | approximate CVP in Schnorr–Adleman prime lattices | a **method** for E2/E3; sufficiency for any approximation factor **not established** | resbarrier (h): |uw| ≥ N − 1 and the lattice-shortness step fails; Ducas 2021 experiments. Details: schnorrcvp |
notes/suffmap_results.md-670-| H10 | Coppersmith / partial-key bounds | **sufficient in the exponential regime only** (X1) | L[α] needs f = O(F_α/x), circular |
notes/suffmap_results.md-671-| H11 | CRT list decoding beyond Johnson | **sufficient for constants** if output-sensitive (C4); a doubly version would be E3 | pilist Prop JR, Remark SEL |
notes/suffmap_results.md-672-| H12 | sub-quadratic sparse linear algebra | **sufficient for a constant** (C5) | Theorem SS(c): single-family sampling ignores ω ≤ 2 |
notes/suffmap_results.md-673-| H13 | factorial / Pochhammer SLPs; τ-conjecture; VP vs VNP | short Pochhammer SLPs (suitable 2-power multiples) are **sufficient** (E4), nonuniform and rigorous. Constant-free, division-free poly-size permanent circuits imply them. The τ-conjecture, if true, *refutes* this route. VP ≠ VNP says nothing about it | Strassen 1976, Lipton 1994, Bürgisser 2009 |
notes/suffmap_results.md-674-| H14 | GRH, RH | **unrelated to speed** | They buy determinism and rigour (Miller; detGRH), not exponents (codex r11: [QRH] gives no gain) |
notes/suffmap_results.md-675-| H15 | P = NP ∩ coNP; BQP ⊆ BPP | **sufficient**, trivially (E5) | |
notes/suffmap_results.md-676-| H16 | RSA inversion vs factoring (Boneh–Venkatesan 1998: no algebraic reduction from factoring to low-degree RSA inversion) | **out of scope** | breaking RSA might be easier than factoring; nothing on this map needs or gives that |
notes/suffmap_results.md-677-
notes/suffmap_results.md-678-**What is *necessary*?**
notes/suffmap_results.md-679-- No *independent structural hypothesis* on the map is known to be necessary for faster factoring. (The
notes/suffmap_results.md-680-  factoring-equivalent invariants of E7 are necessary trivially.) For example, factoring in P is not known to give a
notes/suffmap_results.md-681-  doubly lister in the useful sense: a *fruitful, full-rank set of polynomial-ℓ₁ relations*. Given p and q the trivial
notes/suffmap_results.md-682-  vectors φ(N)·e_i lie in Λ_N but are useless, and polynomial-size ones seem to need DL mod p.
notes/suffmap_results.md-683-- The necessary statements available are model-internal, and they are the barrier literature: Theorem SS(c), resbarrier
notes/suffmap_results.md-684-  C2/ND/GAE, LQ/JR/TAIL.
notes/suffmap_results.md-685-- Theorem SS is an *equivalence within model S*: an L[α] sampling method exists iff a family with C* ≍ F_α exists. MNFS,
notes/suffmap_results.md-686-  unions of pairs and the factory are outside S (§1.1).
