notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-74-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-75-   Schnorr 1991's ℓ1 lattice (weights ℓ_i) has A = ‖·‖₁ exactly. Vera 2010 Thms 1–2 give ℓ_p versions.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:76:2. **Theorem P (promise reduction) [PROVED in the stated parameter regime].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-77-   - If a squarefree witness relation with |w₀| ≤ ω exists, every γ-CVP answer at scale C = e^{(L+A₀)/2}/ω has
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-78-     |w| ≤ ω·γ√(A₀+1)·exp(((γ²−1)A₀+γ²)/2 + R/(2C)).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-79-   - Corollary P1: an exact oracle with a scan over C returns relations.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-80-   - This is the ℓ2/approximate form of Schnorr 1991 Thm 2 and Adleman 1995 §2.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-81-3. **Lemma LA [PROVED].** Testing a GF(2)-kernel *basis* suffices. It factors N deterministically if (a) the relations
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-82-   generate an odd-index sublattice of Λ_N (a strong sufficient condition) and (b) ⟨P⟩ = (Z/N)^*. (b) holds under
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-83-   ERH for B ≥ 2 ln²N when N has no prime factor ≤ B (Bach 1990 Thm 2).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-84-4. **Theorem H (heuristic reduction) [HEURISTIC H_S per target; H_LA; ERH; N not a prime power].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-85-   - Setting: fixed κ > 2, B = (ln N)^κ, n = π(B), targets kN for primes k ∈ (B, 4B].
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-86-   - Then n + 2 pairwise-distinct relations come from O(n·poly L) calls to an exact or γ-CVP oracle, with
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-87-     γ − 1 ≤ c_κ ln B/L.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-88-   - Distinctness is PROVED.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-89-   - So factoring ≤ CVP_{1+n^{−ε}} on these lattices, for any fixed κ > max(2, 1/ε).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-90-   - The witness count is KNOWN (Schnorr 1991 Thm 5, under his "Hypothesis").
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:91:5. **Theorem G (cost vs γ) [MODEL, benign oracle, unit-cost calls].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-92-   - γ = 1 + τL^{2α−1}(ln L)^{1−2α} gives L[α, 2√(ατ)].
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-93-   - With oracle cost n^c this becomes L[α, 2√((1+c)ατ)].
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-94-   - **Conjecture A** (tightness for adversarial oracles; downgraded from "Prop A" after codex found a gap) would make
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-95-     the regime of item 4 the exact one for worst-case oracles.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-96-6. **Prop NP [PROVED from known theorems; folklore].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-97-   - Factoring ≤_T GapCVP_γ for γ ≤ n^{c/lglg n} (DKRS 2003).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-98-   - Factoring ≤_R GapSVP_γ for every constant γ (Khot 2005; Haviv–Regev 2007).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-99-   - So Adleman's 1995 goal was superseded by Ajtai 1998 (SchnorrGate README).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:100:   - An unrefereed 2026 manuscript claims deterministic NP-hardness of GapCVP_{n^{1/400}}.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:101:   - Unknown window: (n^{c/lglg n}, √(n/log n)), or (n^{1/400}, √(n/log n)) if that claim is correct.
