notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-158-**Relation lattice.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-159-- Λ_N = {(a, s) : (−1)^s∏p^a ≡ 1 (mod N)}, with relation vectors exps(u) − exps(|w|).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-160-- The seminorm Σ|a_i|ℓ_i vanishes on (0, 2). So work in the projection π(Λ_N) = {a : ∏p^a ≡ ±1}, of index ≤ φ(N).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-161-- There (v) says every nonzero vector has Σ|a_i|ℓ_i = ln(u|w|) ≥ ln(N − 1).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-162-- Minkowski in R^n gives λ₁(π(Λ_N)) ≤ (n!∏ℓ_i φ(N))^{1/n} ≈ L(ln L + lnln L − 1 + o(1)) for n ≈ L [PROVED; the
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-163-  critic checked it numerically].
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-164-- So relations u ≡ ±w with u|w| ≤ N^{(1+o(1))lnln N} always exist. But v = (u ∓ w)/N is arbitrary, not smooth, so
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-165-  they are relations of Adleman's multiplier form, not vectors of Schnorr's lattice.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-166-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-167-**Gaussian heuristic warning [HEURISTIC].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-168-- For n ≫ L the short vectors are mostly in {0, ±1}^n.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-169-- Ball counts follow smooth-pair counts, which grow like e^{T(1−1/κ)} in ln(uv) ≤ T, not like the volume T^n.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-170-- Ducas (RISC slides 2021-05-20, slide 18): "Gaussian Heuristic seems invalid for certain C".
