notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:174:### 2.1 Theorem P (promise reduction) [PROVED]
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-175-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-176-*Witness.* e⁰ ∈ {0, ±1}^n with A₀ = ln(u₀v₀) and 0 < |w₀| ≤ ω. Set C = e^{(L+A₀)/2}/ω.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-177-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-178-*Claim.* For every γ ≥ 1 and every b(e) with ‖b(e) − t‖ ≤ γ·dist(t, Λ_C):
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-179-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-180-  |w(e)| ≤ ω·R·exp((R² − A₀)/2 + R/(2C)),   R = γ√(A₀+1),  R² − A₀ = (γ²−1)A₀ + γ².
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-181-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-182-*Proof.*
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-183-- |w₀| ≥ e^{(A₀+L)/2}|Δ₀|, so C|Δ₀| ≤ 1 and dist² ≤ A₀ + 1.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-184-- For the answer, A ≤ Q ≤ R² and |Δ| ≤ R/C.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-185-- sinh y ≤ y·e^y for y ≥ 0. ∎
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-186-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-187-Every step was checked by the proof critic and by codex.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-188-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-189-**Corollary P1 (exact oracle, A₀ unknown).**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-190-- Scan j ∈ [⌊L⌋ − 1, A_max], with A_max = poly(L) part of the promise.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-191-- For each j, put ω_j = B·e^{−0.7}/√(j+2) and C_j = e^{(L+j)/2}/ω_j.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-192-- At j = ⌊A₀⌋ (δ = A₀ − j), C_j²Δ₀² ≤ e^{−δ}, and every exact answer has |w| ≤ ω_j√(A₀+1)e^{(δ+e^{−δ})/2}
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-193-  ≤ 0.99·B. So it is a fac-relation, since every integer ≤ B is B-smooth, and w ≠ 0 since N has no factor ≤ B.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-194-- The promise is a witness with |w₀| ≤ ω_{⌊A₀⌋}.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-195-- These are the critic's constants. Our draft's e^{−0.51} with "extra e^{1/2}" did not close.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-196-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-197-**Rounding [PROVED in the regime A₀, A_max = O(L), γ = O(1)].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-198-- Use integer entries round(S√ℓ_i), round(SCℓ_i), round(SCL).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-199-- Q changes by a factor 1 + O(1/S). The last coordinate changes by at most (‖e‖₁+1)/(2S) ≤ (Q/ln 2 + 1)/(2S) in
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-200-  units of CΔ.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-201-- S ≥ L² suffices in this regime. For general heights or γ take S ≫ R³ (codex).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-202-- The logarithms must be certified to that precision. `lattice.py` uses 80-digit mpmath, which covers our toy sizes
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-203-  and is not a general certified construction.
