notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-205-### 2.2 Lemma LA [PROVED]
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-206-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-207-- Relations r₁, …, r_m ∈ Λ_N generate Λ′. K is the GF(2)-kernel of the parity map.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-208-- c ↦ x(c) = (−1)^{y_s}∏p^{y(c)} with y(c) = ½Σc_ir_i is a homomorphism K → μ₂(Z/N). Carries change y by elements
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-209-  of Λ′.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-210-- So a basis suffices to find any x ≠ ±1 in the image.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-211-- If [Λ_N : Λ′] = d is odd, the image is all of μ₂ ∩ ⟨−1, P⟩. If x² = 1 with x = χ(z), then 2dz ∈ Λ′, and the
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-212-  corresponding c gives x^d = x.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-213-- Under ERH, Bach 1990 Thm 2 (primary text, via the literature critic) says a proper subgroup containing all
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-214-  n < x (all units) has x < 2 ln²N. So with N free of prime factors ≤ B and B ≥ 2 ln²N, ⟨P⟩ = (Z/N)^*, which has
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-215-  ≥ 4 square roots of 1.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-216-- Without trial division, use 3 ln²N (Bach Thm 3).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-217-- **Caveat (codex).** Odd index is a strong *sufficient* condition, which we call H_LA. Congruence-of-squares methods
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-218-  can succeed without it, and ERH does not imply it.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-219-- **Code fix.** `squares_dependency_factor` truncated the kernel basis at 64 dependencies by default. Codex
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-220-  constructed a counterexample (N = 35). The default now tests all, and a regression test was added. The E2-P6 runs
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-221-  used the old default and succeeded anyway.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-222-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-223-### 2.3 Distinctness [PROVED] and Adleman's distinctness step [PROVED gap; no prior statement found by us]
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-224-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-225-- **Prime multipliers.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-226-  - Targets ln(kN) for primes k ∈ (B, 4B] give relations u − vkN = w ≡ u (mod N).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-227-  - k ≠ k′ giving the same (u, w) would force vk = v′k′, which is impossible for P-smooth v, v′ and distinct primes
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-228-    k, k′ > B.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-229-  - This proves distinct relations, not independent ones.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-230-- **Adleman 1995 §2.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-231-  - To get different congruences he replaces "V₀ by V₀ + V_i + V_j and rerun[s]", intending to force p_ip_j | P.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-232-  - Since V₀ is a basis vector, this is a unimodular change. The lattice, and hence the set of valid SVP answers, is
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-233-    unchanged (`test_adleman_rerun_lattice_unchanged`). So the literal argument has a gap.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-234-  - A repair (delete V_i, V_j and use target ln(p_ip_jN)) is a *different construction*. It needs its own witness and
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-235-    shortest-vector argument. Its distinctness remains heuristic, because p_ip_j ∈ ⟨P⟩.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-236-  - Searched without finding this observation: Vera 2010, Ducas (README, RISC and PKC slides), crypto.SE 88582,
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-237-    Mulder–Sterner–van Woerden.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-238-  - Not checked (paywalled): Kan–Shen, "On Schnorr–Adleman lattice", PDCAT 2003.
