notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-240-### 2.4 Theorem H [HEURISTIC]
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-241-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-242-**Setting.** Fixed κ > 2, B = (ln N)^κ, n = π(B), targets kN for primes k ∈ (B, 4B] (≥ n + 2 of them).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-243-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-244-**Hypotheses.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-245-- **H_S, for every target** (uniformity is part of the hypothesis): a squarefree witness exists with
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-246-  v ≤ N^a, A₀ ≤ (1 + 2a + o(1))L and |w₀| ≤ ω.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-247-  - Expected witness count under H_S: N^{a(1−2/κ) − 1/κ − o(1)} → ∞ for a > 1/(κ−2).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-248-  - This is Schnorr 1991 Thm 5's count N^{(c−1) − (2c−1)/α}, with his α = κ and c − 1 = a [KNOWN; literature critic].
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-249-- **H_LA.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-250-- **ERH.**
