notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:271:- A *benign* γ-oracle returns a vector whose residual behaves like a random integer of the size allowed by Theorem P,
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-272-  ln|w| ≈ θL + ln B with θ = (γ²−1)(1+2a)/2 → (γ²−1)/2 as a → 0, under the forced local conditions (H_res′).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-273-- With B = L[α, b], each call succeeds with probability exp(−u ln u), u = θL/ln B. We need n relations and n²
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-274-  linear algebra.
