notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-288-**Conjecture A (tightness) [CONJECTURED].** If (γ² − 1)A₀ ≫ ln B, the γ-ball around t contains non-relations, so an
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-289-adversarial oracle defeats this query strategy.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-290-- **Why "Prop A" was withdrawn (codex, FATAL to the claim).** The draft used radius γ√(A₀+1), but the true distance d
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-291-  may be much smaller than the witness bound. Also, A ≈ γ²A₀ does not give Q ≈ A without squarefreeness, and the
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-292-  §3 shell counts do not show *non-smooth* vectors inside the admissible ball jointly over the C-scan.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-293-- A proof needs actual-distance bounds and a joint count inside the ball.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-294-- Even if true, it would say nothing about other lattices or embeddings.
