notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-388-## 4. Schnorr 2021, dissected
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-389-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-390-Text read: "corrected" ePrint 2021/933, PDF dated 16.06.2021 (ePrint page: received 2021-07-09), via web.archive.org.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-391-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-392-1. **The claim.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-393-   - n = 47 / 95 for 400 / 800 bits.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-394-   - One fac-relation per random permutation f.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-395-   - Block size 24; 4.2·10⁹ and 8.4·10^{10} operations.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-396-   - "This destroys the RSA cryptosystem."
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-397-   - At 800 bits he derives |u − vN| ≲ 522.9 ≈ p_n^{1.0075}, assuming v ≲ p_n, and writes "ρ(0.007544) = 0.991". In
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-398-     the standard normalisation that is ρ(1.0075) ≈ 0.99.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-399-2. **Algebraic failures [PROVED; primary text checked]. These alone invalidate the proof.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-400-   - Lemma 3.1's proof concludes "u − vN′ < v|ẑ|/(1 − ε/2)". The correct conclusion is
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-401-     |u − vN| < (N/N′)·v|ẑ|/(1 − ε/2), so the factor N^{n/(n+1)} is missing.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-402-     - **KNOWN:** Daniel S, crypto.SE answer 88601 (update of 16 March 2021): the bounds are on |u − vN′|, "of very
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-403-       different size" from the |u − vN| that must be smooth.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-404-     - Codex (schnorrcvp_1) and we make the missing factor explicit (Theorem R(ii)).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-405-   - "‖b₁‖ < 0.917" is impossible: every nonzero vector of L(R_{n,f}) has a coordinate |f(i)e_i| ≥ 1, or norm
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-406-     ≥ N′ ln N.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-407-     - Daniel S (same answer) recomputed the bound as ≈ 5.67·10^{10}.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-408-     - The "norm ≥ 1" argument is codex's; no prior statement was found by the critic.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-409-   - (3.3) "‖b‖² ≥ ln uv + ẑ²" holds for diagonal √ln p_i, not for the displayed f(i). A coordinate with f(i) = 1 and
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-410-     p_i > e contradicts it.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-411-   - Context: kodlu and Daniel S on a determinant error in the March 3 version; Couteau (88590) on reliance on flawed
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-412-     pruning estimates.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-413-3. **What exists [MODEL, H_S].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-414-   - His 800-bit box (v ≤ 499, |w| ≤ 523) holds an expected **3.7·10^{−176}** relations. The analogous 400-bit box
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-415-     (v ≤ 211, |w| ≤ 250) is our construction, not his: 9.2·10^{−85}.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:416:   - Over all sizes the totals are 1.5·10^{−115} and 1.4·10^{−52}.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-417-   - The mechanism is |uw| ≥ N − 1: with |w| ≤ 523, u is a 499-smooth integer ≥ N/523. Their density near 2^{800} is
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-418-     3.6·10^{−180} (model), and there are 10^{62.2–62.35} of them below 2^{800} (bracket).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-419-   - This is heuristic. It says that, under the standard smoothness model, the required relations should not exist
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-420-     at these parameters. Combined with item 2, the claim has neither a valid proof nor a plausible mechanism.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-421-4. **SVP embedding.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-422-   - Ducas tested the **March 3 version** (scale N, not N′): 0 relations in 1000 trials at 400 bits with n = 47.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-423-     Exponent vectors were "typically very sparse, say a single 1 and a single −1".
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-424-   - Only last coefficient ±1 is useful, and the paper never enforces it: ccorn (crypto.SE 88647) and Vera's
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-425-     Remark 6.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-426-   - Short vectors with last coefficient 0 correspond to smooth near-twins (Mulder–Sterner–van Woerden 2025 §1:
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-427-     "the shortest vectors in the prime number lattice often correspond to smooth twins").
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-428-   - "Shortest vectors always have last coefficient 0" is not a theorem (codex). It is the typical behaviour at
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-429-     Schnorr's parameters.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-430-5. **Cost with lattice algorithms [SCENARIO].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-431-   - **Asymptotic.** If CVP with γ = 1 + O(1) costs 2^{Θ(n)} and n ≥ n_min ≈ (ln N)^{3/2+o(1)}, the cost is
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-432-     exp((ln N)^{3/2+o(1)}). With multiplier targets it is exp(Θ(L lnL/lnlnL)). This is a scenario under stated
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-433-     assumptions, not a lower bound for specialised algorithms.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-434-   - **β-dependence.** BKZ-β has root-Hermite factor δ_β ≈ (β/2πe)^{1/(2(β−1))}. Under a GSA-type scenario,
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-435-     Babai/enumeration on a BKZ-β basis gives residuals that blow up like N^{Θ(γ_β²)} unless β approaches n.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-436-     - Codex warns that a root-Hermite factor is not a CVP ratio relative to the actual target distance. So this is a
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-437-       sensitivity scenario only.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-438-     - At toy n ≤ 40 (E2), LLL-Babai outputs had median |w| ≈ N^{0.64}. Ten LLL-Babai outputs had u or v with more
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-439-       than 4000 bits.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-440-   - **Concrete (E0b) [SCENARIO].**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-441-     - log₂T = 0.292n + max(0, log₂V − 0.2075n), where V(n) is the number of lattice vectors an ideal unit-cost
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-442-       enumerator (increasing |w|) must output to see n + 1 relations.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-443-     - V uses naive H_S and counts non-coprime (u, v) too, so its direction of bias is not established (codex).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-444-     - The sieve's 2^{0.2075n} close vectors per call are an idealisation.
