notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-471-## 5. Rigour map (Q2)
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-472-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-473-| Step | Status |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-474-|---|---|
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-475-| Theorem R; λ₁(π(Λ_N)) bounds | PROVED |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:476:| Theorem P + Corollary P1 (+ rounding, in the stated regime) | PROVED |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-477-| Distinctness via primes k > B | PROVED |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-478-| Lemma LA (kernel basis; odd index + ERH ⇒ factor) | PROVED (conditional) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-479-| Witness for every target (smooth u within ≈ B/√L of smooth multiples of kN) | HEURISTIC H_S; a smooth-numbers-in-short-intervals statement far beyond known results; Schnorr 1991's "Hypothesis" |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-480-| Odd index | HEURISTIC H_LA (strong sufficient condition) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-481-| Benign-oracle residual smoothness | HEURISTIC H_res′ (E2: ratio 0.87 pre-registered, 1.29 normalised) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:482:| Theorem G | MODEL |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-483-| Conjecture A (tightness) | CONJECTURED |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-484-| E0 counts / n_min | MODEL (naive H_S) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-485-| BKZ / E0b costs | SCENARIO |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-486-| Prop NP | PROVED from cited theorems (folklore) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-487-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-488-**Cleanest provable statement.** Let N not be a prime power, with no prime factor ≤ B, B ≥ 2 ln²N, and assume ERH.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-489-Assume (i) for each of n + 2 primes k ∈ (B, 4B] a squarefree witness exists for target kN, with A₀ ≤ poly(L) and
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-490-|w₀| ≤ ω_{⌊A₀⌋}; and (ii) the relations generate an odd-index sublattice of Λ_N. Then an exact-CVP oracle on the prime
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-491-lattices of dimension n = π(B) factors N in deterministic polynomial time with O(n·poly L) calls. Under H_S, (i) needs
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-492-B = (ln N)^κ with κ > 2. B ≥ 2 ln²N is only the linear-algebra floor.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-493-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-494-## 6. Variants (Q5)
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-495-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-496-| Variant | Effect | Cost / status |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-497-|---|---|---|
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-498-| Multiplier targets ln(kN), v free | shells positive for κ > 1; rigorous distinctness for k > B | N^{Ω(1)} targets when κ < 3/2; SCENARIO exp(Θ(L lnL/lnlnL)) with 2^{Θ(n)} CVP |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-499-| Adleman SVP form u − kN^γ = w | same relations | its distinctness step has a gap (§2.3); same cost |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:500:| ℓ1 / ℓ_p / other weights | log\|w\| stays linear in the norm of e | Theorem P-type upper bound PROVED (Vera's ℓ_p versions); tightness CONJECTURED |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-501-| Enlarged residual base B₂ (Yan, Grebnev) | raises the yield per output | not modelled here; changes constants and dimension, not the 2^{Θ(n)} premise (assessment) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-502-| NFS rational side via prime lattices | a poly-delay enumerator of dimension L[1/3] would give the factory constant 1.6386 (smoothenum T3) | HYPOTHETICAL; known enumeration is exp(L[1/3]) |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-503-| Algebraic side (S-unit lattice CVP) | toward smoothenum T6/T7 | SPECULATIVE: needs S-unit/class-group data plus principality, dimension L[1/3] |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-504-| Two lattices (u-side and w-side) | w = u − vN is not multiplicative in e, so w-smoothness cannot be imposed linearly | assessment |
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-505-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-506-No variant is plausibly better.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-507-- Only a *polynomial-time* CVP_{1+n^{−ε}} algorithm on this family gives polynomial-time factoring (Theorem H).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-508-- A 2^{n^c} algorithm at n = L^κ gives exp(L^{κc}).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-509-- No converse reduction is known.
