notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-551-- **E2-P1 to E2-P4 passed** as pre-registered:
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-552-  - pooled 0.87 ∈ [1/2, 2];
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-553-  - refined fits better than naive;
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-554-  - yield at 40 bits < yield at 20 bits in every cell;
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-555-  - median log₂|w|/bits for S21 at ≥ 32 bits is 0.96 / 0.92.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-556-- **Predictor defect (codex #18; disclosed).**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-557-  - The pre-registered predictor gave 2066 probabilities > 1 (up to 12.7), and 66 relations had p = 0. It multiplied
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-558-    real-interval densities by local factors without discrete normalisation.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-559-  - The POST-HOC normalised predictor (`analyze.corrected_e2`) uses exact discrete probabilities for |w| ≤ 2·10⁵:
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-560-    smooth and coprime-to-supp(uv) among the window's integers coprime to supp(uv); 1 for |w| ≤ B. Larger |w| is
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-561-    clipped. It gives **1.29 pooled** (1.21–1.78).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-562-  - The remaining excess matches E1's parity effect, which the coprime-only predictor omits.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-563-  - Conclusion: residuals of CVP outputs are smooth at roughly the rate of random integers of their size with the
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-564-    forced local conditions, within ×1.8. E2 tests smoothness given the observed residual. It does not test whether
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:565:    approximate answers saturate Theorem P's bound.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-566-- **Yield per list output.**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-567-  - n = 40, A1.0: 0.82 / 0.66 / 0.50 / 0.40 / 0.16 / 0.085 at 20–40 bits.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-568-  - n = 40, S21sqrt: 0.18 → 0.000.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-569-  - Exact-CVP (list0) residuals for A-variants have median |w| ≈ N^{0.475}.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-570-- **E2-P5.** 700 list0 relations, of which 416 distinct (59%). Random weights do not guarantee distinctness (as
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-571-  Aboumrad–Widdows–Kaushik observed). Prime multipliers do (§2.3).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-572-- **E2-P6 (correctness only).**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-573-  - All 15 N of 20–36 bits were factored from pooled relations. Factors are STRUCTURAL: N's prime factors exceed
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-574-    p₄₀ = 173.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-575-  - At 40 bits, only 17–22 distinct relations were found (< 42).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-576-- **Certification of list0 (codex #19).**
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-577-  - list0 is "closest found", not certified exact. Targets enter fplll's enumeration as binary64.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-578-  - Spot check (`check_list0.py`, 100 random lattices) against fplll `CVP.closest_vector(method="proved")`:
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-579-    - 91 agree;
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-580-    - in 8, list0 is strictly *closer*, so fplll's "proved" mode is not exact on these large-entry lattices;
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-581-    - in 1 (40 bits, n = 30, A1.25), list0 missed the closest vector (distance ratio 2.53).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-582-- **Deviation.** The first E2 run crashed on a Babai output with u > 10^{4300}. We patched serialization and reran
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-583-  deterministically; the crashed log is kept.
