notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-597-## 8. Coordination
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-598-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-599-**suffmap** (H9: "sufficiency for any approximation factor not established; details: schnorrcvp"). Our answer:
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-600-- sufficient for polynomial time at γ = 1 + n^{−ε} (Theorem H; heuristic);
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:601:- sufficient for L[α < 1/3] at γ = 1 + (log n)^{−c}, c > 1 (benign oracle, Theorem G);
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-602-- for γ fixed > 1, L[1/2, √(γ²−1)] (benign);
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-603-- nothing guaranteed at growing γ.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-604-- Near-exact prime-lattice CVP is an instance of suffmap's E3 (Bohr-set lister over all smooth multipliers v), so it
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-605-  inherits Prop DLT (it would also give prime-field DL, as Schnorr 1991's title suggests).
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md:606:- **Consistency with suffmap's Prop SI (1.2114).** Prop SI fixes v = 1, so its residual must span the smooth-number
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-607-  gap 1/d(kN), which sets the constant. Schnorr's lattice ranges over N^{o(1)} smooth v, so witnesses with |w| ≤ B
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-608-  exist and the floor is paid by the γ = 1 + o(1) oracle instead.
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-609-
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-610-**abcsunit.** Relations are S-unit solutions of u − vN = w. Evertse 1984 bounds λx + μy = 1 by 3·7^{d+2s} (s = |S|
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-611-including ∞), i.e. 3·7^{2s+3} over Q with s finite primes. That is 2^{O(n)}, far above n + 1, so finiteness is no
notes/schnorrcvp_results.md-612-obstruction. The obstruction is the small-height count of §3.
