   364	**What the experiments show.** The laws behind the negative analysis hold at toy size: (h + 1)/N per oblivious pair
   365	regardless of K (E1, E2), and smoothness of the tested part exactly at its size (E3). They do not and cannot show
   366	asymptotic statements. MITM and 2-D aim are excellent at toy sizes only because toy h is a large power of N.
