   373	## 8. Reviews
   374	- **Codex blind round** (`codex/siconstruct_1.out`, GPT-6.1-sol, xhigh, run before our analysis was written down).
   375	  It reached the same verdict independently: interval sieve L[2/3, 2/(3κ)]; construct-one-factor-and-test has a
   376	  cofactor ≥ N/h (its version of Lemma RC); two explicit sorted lists cost N^{1/2+o(1)} per output for
   377	  L[1/3, O(1)] outputs (its version of Lemma MA, with the exact sorted-list accounting Õ(m + n + Km + H));
   378	  Wagner's tree violates M^r ≤ KN for r ≥ 4; Boneh's and GSS's recovery conditions fail by a huge factor; exact
   379	  CVP costs 2^{m+o(m)} (ADS 2015, Cor. 6.5, checked by codex), m = L[1/3, κ]. Items we adopted:
   380	  - a *binary* embedding e_p = Σ2^j z_{p,j} that enforces e ≥ 0, for which exact CVP solves Prop SI and
   381	    γ² ≤ 1 + 3/(m + 1) suffices (an alternative to Prop CV that handles non-squarefree outputs; dimension
   382	    m = O(π(y) ln x));
   383	  - the fixed-κ threshold τ < 0.6905 (§1);
   384	  - the diversity caveat (§5);
   385	  - the counting-to-search reduction, the precision obstruction for approximate counts, the log-grid DP bound and the
   386	    Jain and Bach–Sorenson references (§4.6).
   387	  Codex labels general non-existence UNVERIFIED, as we do: these are barriers for named method classes.
   388	
   389	## 9. Reproduction
   390	```
   391	.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_siconstruct.py
   392	.venv/bin/python -m src.siconstruct.run_exp E1   # ~1 min
   393	.venv/bin/python -m src.siconstruct.run_exp E2   # ~10 min, < 1 GB
   394	.venv/bin/python -m src.siconstruct.run_exp E3   # ~5 min
   395	.venv/bin/python -m src.siconstruct.diag_e3      # ~5 min (post-hoc)
   396	```

