391-## 3. Construction attempts (Task 3)
392-
393-### 3.1 Whole-box multivariate decoders
394-
395-**Linear forms (rational side).**
396-- Herrmann–May (ASIACRYPT 2008, Thm 4; under their Assumption 1, with ε slack): ∏X_i < P^{g_n(μ)}, where
397-  g_n(μ) = (n+1)μ − n + n(1 − μ)^{1+1/n}.
398-- **g_n(μ) ≤ μ² [PROVED].** With a = 1 − μ, μ² − g_n(μ) = a[(n − 1) + a − n·a^{1/n}] ≥ 0 by AM–GM (codex; checked
399-  to 10⁻¹⁴ on a grid).
400-- So the Herrmann–May decoder, and any 2-D decoder whose range is at most theirs, satisfies (J) with V = the box.
401:  Prop JR then applies: **Γ_cert = L^{o(1)}** [model-PROVED, conditional on HM's heuristic for the range].
402-- Caveats (critic M4):
403-  - HM is stated for inhomogeneous linear f. For the homogeneous G = Y₁a + Y₀b the algebraic-independence step
404-    degenerates (only a/b is determined) and needs a separate check.
405-  - Nothing here bounds *all* 2-D certificates.
406-- Not covered: whole-box decoders whose range exceeds HM's. None is known to us.
407-
408-**Algebraic side (degree δ) and doubly-smooth decoders.**
409-- (J) has D = δ, a smaller range. Jochemsz–May (Assumption 1) treats known moduli, so its use for unknown divisors
410-  is an extrapolation of their strategy.
411-- The JR proof applies with ρ_q ≤ δ roots per prime, provided root counts behave on average as the prime ideal
412-  theorem predicts. The worst case ω(P) log δ is not o(F).
413-- HEURISTIC.
414-
415-**Cost in smoothenum's model.** 1.9019 (gain L^{o(1)}). Codex's batch condition, ω − κ ≥ θr, fails for the class.
416-
417-### 3.2 GS / PV / folded / multiplicity CRT decoding
418-
419:- **Within Johnson** (GRS; Boneh; GSS with weights and multiplicities): Prop JR, L^{o(1)}.
420-- **Beyond Johnson.**
421-  - What would suffice is output-sensitive listing of {z : smooth part ≥ y^{θ'}} with the full factor base. By
422-    Remark SEL (c) that is a partial lister. So this open item is not a separate lever: within Johnson it is
423-    closed conditionally (JR); beyond it, it is the crux.
424-  - Known beyond-Johnson decoders (folded RS; multiplicity codes; plain RS, Brakensiek et al. 2026 preprint, §2.3) work at
425-    fixed rate, with n^{O_ε(1)} lists and time that blows up as agreement → 0. None is a CRT decoder for the vanishing-rate regime here.
426-- **Cost:** within Johnson 1.9019; beyond, HYPOTHETICAL c(θ') from Table 1.1.
