700-  outputs lie on five divisor lattices whose shortest vectors are multiples of (30, 1): (−60, −2), (−300, −10),
701-  (−150, −5), (210, 7), (−420, −14).
702-- G(30, 1) = 30Y₁ + Y₀ has a large P-part, and the multiples k·(30, 1) inherit it. So the excess comes from
703-  non-primitive points. This diagnosis removes the specific discrepancy; it does not prove the conditional model.
704-- Restricted to gcd(a, b) = 1, with the primitive (projective) density Pr[q | G] = 1/(q + 1), the cells
705-  with pred_coprime ≥ 10 give observed/predicted 0.84, 0.64, 1.25, 1.12, 0.59, 1.25 and 0.40.
706-  - Total: 85 against 96.2, 0.88. The z-cells share points, so this is not a sum of independent counts.
