708-    4.98.
709-  - The density is exact on average over uniform primitive pairs. Per row it is 1/q for q ∤ b and 0 for q | b,
710-    which consecutive rows average correctly.
711:- The 1/(q + 1) density only lowers the probabilities, so Prop JR's hypothesis Pr[v_q ≥ j] ≤ q^{−j} is
712-  conservative for primitive points.
