533-**Verdict — UNVERIFIED for Prop SI.** The proposed factoring constant is sound under residual randomness, charged preprocessing and adequate relation diversity. The checked methods leave a specific unresolved task: engineering a smooth product at exponentially fine relative precision while keeping its height near \(N\). Explicit-list reuse does not amortise enough, standard birthday representations lack the required admissible input domains, CRT decoding lies outside its recovery range, and constructing one large smooth factor leaves either a nearly \(N\)-sized cofactor or a severe placement search. These are concrete barriers for the stated models; they do not constitute a general impossibility theorem.
