    37	  is the same leading cost as sieving the interval, so the 1.2114 target collapses to L[2/3] per relation.
    38	  - In the sampling/sieving model the whole relation program then costs L[1/2, √2].
    39	  - Meet-in-the-middle costs exponentially much, and lattice reduction costs exp(L[1/3]).
